; PineTree2 — 6th Forest tree pick, added 2026-08-26 (content-variety pass, Task 5). A
; SECOND conifer pick alongside the existing PineTree.tscn — same reasoning PineTree.tscn
; itself used against CommonTree1/CommonTree2 (same-height-different-shape reads better
; than a near-duplicate), applied one level deeper: matched canopy HEIGHT to the rest of
; the set, but a deliberately NARROWER footprint than PineTree.tscn so the two conifers
; don't read as the same silhouette repeated.
;
; Source: "Pine_2.fbx", Textured Stylized Trees (May 2020) by Quaternius, CC0 1.0
; Universal — License.txt at `source-content/assets/Textured Stylized Trees - May 2020.../
; License.txt` re-checked before import, per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate (states
; CC0 1.0 Universal / Public Domain Dedication, same boilerplate as every other Quaternius
; pack in this repo). Recorded in the newly-authored
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_textured_stylized_trees.tres (same pack as
; DeadTree.tscn, extended rather than duplicated).
;
; SCALE (NON-UNIFORM — the one variant in this pass that isn't a plain uniform rescale):
; the source file bakes a 90-degree axis correction + scale=100 into its own child node
; (Blender Z-up -> FBX Y-up, same mechanism PineTree.tscn's header documents), measured
; post-correction global AABB height = 8.3438 units, footprint 6.6126 x 6.7847 at that
; height — i.e. this raw asset is a naturally BUSHY/wide pine (footprint/height ratio
; ~0.79-0.81), unlike PineTree.glb's naturally narrow/tapered raw proportions
; (~0.35-0.38 ratio). A uniform rescale to the ~2.5-tile height target used by every other
; Forest tree would therefore produce a ~2.0-tile-wide canopy — nearly 2.5x PineTree.tscn's
; own scaled footprint (0.883 x 0.960) and badly overflowing a 1x1 tile. To hit BOTH the
; ~2.5-tile height target from the task table AND a footprint narrower than PineTree.tscn's
; (the explicit ask), this scene applies a non-uniform scale: Y = 0.300 (2.5 / 8.3438,
; height) and X/Z = 0.096 (0.65 / 6.7847, footprint capped PRE-ROTATION at ~0.65 on the raw
; axis) — giving a scaled footprint of ~0.635 x 0.651, narrower than PineTree.tscn's
; ~0.88 x 0.96 as asked. Those scaled numbers are also the SHIPPED world-space footprint
; here, unlike the crop scenes' capped numbers: this Model node carries a scale-only
; transform with no rotation, so there is no diagonal-widening jitter to account for (see
; cultivated_field.tres's header for the rotated case).
; FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, not a measured GDD number — FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF: this is a genuine judgment call, and unlike the plain rescales used everywhere
; else in this pass, a non-uniform stretch changes the raw mesh's proportions (flattens a
; naturally bushy pine into a narrower profile) rather than preserving them, which is a
; different kind of risk to the "out-of-the-box silhouettes ship as-is" policy (art.md) —
; worth a specific eyeball check for whether the squash reads as an intentional narrow
; conifer or as a visibly distorted mesh.
;
; SLAB IS 1.0x0.2x1.0 (matches every current-generation terrain slab, post the
; "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0" cross-tile seam fix PineTree.tscn's header documents).
;
; FLOOR TREATMENT MATCHES EVERY OTHER FOREST VARIANT EXACTLY (same slab tint, same 3-patch
; moss/litter blotch treatment, same relative transforms) so a Forest tile's floor reads
; identically regardless of which of the now-6 trees it lands on.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (required, not cosmetic): identical
; OcclusionFader exemption requirement as every sibling terrain scene — see
; CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full mechanism. The ground plane (renamed "Ground")
; and all 3 floor patches are children of a wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab".
;
; MATERIAL OVERRIDE ADDED (2026-08-26, human-reported bug: "some of the trees are just
; plain white") — same root cause and same fix as DeadTree.tscn (see that file's header for
; the full mechanism): "Textured Stylized Trees" ships real textures, but only the raw
; .fbx was copied at import time, so both of this mesh's surfaces ("Bark", "Pine_Leaves")
; fell back to Godot's near-white default (measured albedo_color 0.9063/0.9063/0.9063 on
; both). Fixed via `surface_material_override` on the instanced FBX's "Pine_2" mesh node,
; matching Rabbit.tscn's precedent: `Tree_Bark.jpg` (this pack's generic bark texture — no
; pine-specific bark exists) for surface 0, `Pine_Leaves.png` for surface 1, both copied to
; this directory, both overrides with `vertex_color_use_as_albedo` explicitly false.
; `[editable path="Model"]` is required for the override to apply to a node living inside an
; instanced sub-scene.
[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

